  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">Les cadres r&#xE9;glementaire et institutionnel de la protection sociale  sont renforc&#xE9;s</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="FR">The ILO&apos;s programme in Burundi aims to reinforce the country&apos;s social protection system, ensuring more inclusive and equitable coverage for its population. Despite recent advancements, a significant portion of the Burundian population, particularly those in the informal economy, remains excluded from essential social security benefits, including health coverage and cash transfers. The programme supports the implementation of the ILO Flagship Programme on Building Social Protection Floors for All, focusing on enhancing universal social protection through improved governance, financing, and institutional capacity.
The main objectives of the programme include revising Burundi&apos;s National Social Protection Policy (PNPS) and strategy, advocating for social protection as a key component of the National Development Plan, and building the capacity of national actors to effectively implement and sustain social protection schemes. These efforts will be aligned with the country&#x2019;s poverty reduction goals and the Sustainable Development Goals, particularly SDG 1 (End poverty) and SDG 3 (Ensure healthy lives and promote well-being).
The programme involves collaboration with national government institutions, employers&apos; and workers&apos; organizations, as well as regional and global partners. It also focuses on strengthening data systems for social protection and promoting regional knowledge-sharing to enhance policy-making and institutional capacity across the Great Lakes Region.
Through this initiative, the ILO aims to improve access to essential social services, reduce vulnerability, and strengthen the resilience of the most marginalized groups, contributing to a more just and inclusive social protection system in Burundi.</narrative>
  </description>
